       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A dose like that risks serious hepatotoxicity, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total). This is probably the most likely intent.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day).\n- **500 to 1,000 mg PO every 6 to 8 hours as needed**, with a stated daily maximum.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the order with your resident or attending, and check whether the patient is getting acetaminophen from other sources, such as combination products."
